Chapter: Fat16Subdir
  cites Foreword chapter Fat16

 A Codex program can write a file into a subdirectory, and this
 is the test that says so. fat16-create-file used to refuse any path with a
 separator in it -- honestly, while the parent-directory walk was unwritten,
 because dropping "SUB/NOTE.TXT" into the root under the name "SUB" would have
 been worse than saying no.

 The write and the read-back share no code. fat16-write-file goes through
 fat16-create-in-subdir, which resolves the parent with the READ side's own
 fat16-walk-path and then hands a byte address to the same fat16-create-at-slot
 the root path uses. fat16-read-text walks the directory and follows the
 cluster chain to get the bytes back.

 The assertion that matters most is not "wrote True" -- it is that NOTE.TXT is
 NOT in the root. A writer that quietly ignored the parent and created the leaf
 in the root would report success and read back nothing through the subdirectory
 path, so a test that only checked the round trip through SUB/ would look
 identical whether the parent was honoured or discarded. Reading the root is
 what tells the two apart.

 The refusals are pinned too, because both are ways this can silently corrupt a
 volume rather than fail: a parent that does not exist, and a parent that
 resolves to a FILE (whose entry would otherwise be written into the file's own
 data cluster, corrupting it and producing an entry no walk would ever find).

 The fixture is built host-side by build/make-fat16-subdir.ps1, from the FAT16
 spec rather than from this chapter. That independence is the point: a fixture
 written by the code under test proves only that the code agrees with itself,
 which is exactly how a CCE short name would round-trip forever here while
 being unreadable to every other FAT driver on earth. The harness also checks
 the raw bytes host-side.

 We say:

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console, Device.Block] Nothing
  opening = act
    ok <- fat16-write-file "SUB/NOTE.TXT" "hello subdir"
    print-line-uni ("wrote " & show ok)

    vol <- fat16-init 2048
    back <- fat16-read-text vol "SUB/NOTE.TXT"
    print-line-uni ("readback " & maybe-text back)

    root <- fat16-read-text vol "NOTE.TXT"
    print-line-uni ("not-in-root " & maybe-text root)

    entry <- fat16-resolve-path vol "SUB/NOTE.TXT"
    print-line-uni ("size " & show (entry-size entry))

    miss <- fat16-write-file "NOPE/X.TXT" "no parent"
    print-line-uni ("no-parent " & show miss)

    onfile <- fat16-write-file "SUB/NOTE.TXT/X.TXT" "parent is a file"
    print-line-uni ("parent-is-file " & show onfile)

    deep <- fat16-write-file "ROOT.TXT" "still works"
    print-line-uni ("root-still-works " & show deep)
  end

Section: Reporting

  maybe-text : Maybe Text -> Text
  maybe-text (m) = when m
    is Just (t) -> t
    is None -> "<none>"

  entry-size : Maybe Fat16DirEntry -> Integer
  entry-size (m) = when m
    is Just (e) -> e.de-size
    is None -> 0 - 1
